<info>
  <ul>
    <li>Template written in Slim instead of HTML - detected from its first line, or forced with a <code>&lt;slim&gt;</code> block as here</li>
    <li>Tags nest by indentation, <code>.class</code> / <code>#id</code> shorthand (a bare <code>.card</code> is a div), Tailwind classes like <code>p-0.5</code>, <code>w-1/2</code>, <code>bg-[#fff]</code> stay in the shorthand</li>
    <li>Control flow: <code>- if</code>, <code>- else</code>, <code>- each list as item</code> or <code>- list.each do |item|</code></li>
    <li>Output: <code>= expr</code>, <code>== raw_html</code>, text lines start with <code>|</code></li>
    <li>Nodes are joined without whitespace - space things with CSS <code>gap</code> / margin</li>
    <li><code>fez compile -t file.fez</code> prints the generated template with source lines</li>
